{"team":"KC","col":"#FF4D57","identity":"pass-heavy","funnel":"balanced-D","plays_pg":61.5,"adot":7.1,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Air Raid</h2><p>This is an aggressive, pass-leaning attack: <strong>+5%</strong> pass rate over expected, top of the league's range, and no interest in sitting on a lead (50% pass when ahead).</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>There's no bell-cow to bank on \u2014 the lead back sees just <strong>50%</strong> of carries (league ~59%), a committee that caps any one back's ceiling and makes their rushing props matchup- and script-dependent.</p><p><strong>Travis Kelce</strong> is a genuine centerpiece, not an afterthought \u2014 <strong>22%</strong> of targets (league ~15%).</p><p>They spread the ball as much as anyone \u2014 the WR1 commands only <strong>16%</strong> of targets (league ~23%). Volume is democratic here, which suppresses any single receiver's ceiling but props up the TE and secondary options.</p><p>They live in the shotgun (80% of snaps vs ~68%) \u2014 a spread, pass-oriented structure.</p><p>When they fall behind they abandon the run entirely \u2014 61% pass while trailing, so their pass-catchers have huge comeback-script ceilings.</p><p><strong>Patrick Mahomes</strong> is a scramble threat \u2014 he takes off on <strong>4.8%</strong> of dropbacks (nearly double the 3.3% norm), rushing production that both lifts his own yardage and siphons a few carries from the backfield.</p><p>By the numbers it's an efficient unit \u2014 a 46% success rate (above the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Their red-zone identity is <strong>pass-first</strong> (56% pass), which puts scoring equity on <strong>Rashee Rice</strong>. And with the TE commanding 22% of targets, <strong>Travis Kelce</strong> is a live red-zone option too.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 No Obvious Seam</h2><p>They lock down opposing WR1s \u2014 just 50 rec yds/game (vs ~58); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They surrender <strong>108 rushing</strong> and <strong>220 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). No dominant funnel \u2014 read it matchup by matchup.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: <strong>Rashee Rice</strong> holds value even when they're winning; their pass-catchers have massive ceilings in comeback scripts (fade-material as underdogs).</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Patrick Mahomes","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":13,"props":{"Comp":23.15,"Att":34.56,"Pass Yds":253.99,"Pass TD":1.83,"INT":0.61,"Rush Yds":20.74},"d":{"completions":23.15,"attempts":34.56,"pass_yards":253.99,"pass_td":1.83,"interceptions":0.61,"rush_att":3.63,"rush_yards":20.74}}],"RB":[{"name":"Kenneth Walker III","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":44,"props":{"Rush Att":15.12,"Rush Yds":65.21,"Tgt":3.43,"Rec":2.86,"Rec Yds":21.92},"d":{"rush_att":15.12,"rush_yards":65.21,"targets":3.43,"receptions":2.86,"rec_yards":21.92,"rec_td":0.06}},{"name":"Emari Demercado","slot":"RB2","starter":true,"td":15,"props":{"Rush Att":5.08,"Rush Yds":32.21,"Tgt":2.32,"Rec":1.75,"Rec Yds":12.06},"d":{"rush_att":5.08,"rush_yards":32.21,"targets":2.32,"receptions":1.75,"rec_yards":12.06,"rec_td":0.05}},{"name":"Emmett Johnson","slot":"RB3","starter":false,"td":15,"props":{"Rush Att":2.62,"Rush Yds":11.04,"Tgt":1.3,"Rec":0.88,"Rec Yds":6.24},"d":{"rush_att":2.62,"rush_yards":11.04,"targets":1.3,"receptions":0.88,"rec_yards":6.24,"rec_td":0.04}},{"name":"Brashard Smith","slot":"RB4","starter":false,"td":13,"props":{"Rush Att":3.03,"Rush Yds":11.24,"Tgt":2.34,"Rec":1.5,"Rec Yds":10.55},"d":{"rush_att":3.03,"rush_yards":11.24,"targets":2.34,"receptions":1.5,"rec_yards":10.55,"rec_td":0.07}}],"WR":[{"name":"Rashee Rice","slot":"WR1","starter":true,"td":39,"props":{"Tgt":9.12,"Rec":6.79,"Rec Yds":75.89,"Rec TD":0.49},"d":{"targets":9.12,"receptions":6.79,"rec_yards":75.89,"rec_td":0.49}},{"name